Keep Windows native views in step with GPUI's frame: present it through a composition surface while a view shows.

What: While a view shows, GPUI's frame is rendered into its swap chain's back buffer as always, then copied into a
DirectComposition surface (`IDCompositionSurface::BeginDraw`/`EndDraw`) that GPUI's visual shows instead of the
swap chain (`native_view_surface.rs`, one table `native_views::present_step`): a surface changes only on `Commit`,
while a swap chain's `Present` and a `Commit` are not atomic, so through the surface GPUI's frame, its holes and the
views' placement change in one `Commit`. With no view shown the swap chain presents as upstream (no copy, no commit).
The surface is left over two frames, so no stale swap chain frame flashes: the frame the last view goes is still
copied into the surface and committed with the views' removal, and presented to the swap chain too; the next frame
presents and shows the swap chain again, which already holds that hole-less frame. The switch either way is logged
at info. The surface is premultiplied, as 0056's swap chain is. The code is in a new file,
`directx_renderer/native_view_surface.rs` (swap chain or surface), plus the `present_step` table in 0057's
`native_views.rs`; 0057's `present_native_views` shows each frame through it, and `directx_renderer.rs` gets only
the module row.

Why: A frame that moves a view keeps hole and view in step
(owner decision 2026-11-27: with the swap chain alone, about one frame in 20–40 of a sliding view showed a 3 px gap).
The cost is one GPU copy of GPUI's own frame and one `Commit` per GPUI frame while a view shows, never per frame of
a view's content (an idle window draws no GPUI frame, so copies nothing); a window with no view shown pays nothing.

Test: `native_views.rs`'s `present_steps` table (the present step per (showing, views) pair) runs on any host through
`scripts/patch-test.sh` (windows-pure). Live, in 0057's `scripts/windows-native-view-checks.sh`: no gap colour in
any of 100 screenshots while the view slides, nor after a resize; one surface copy per GPUI frame while it slides;
0 copies per second while only the view presents; the alpha mode is logged.

Upstream PR: not filed (filing paused, patch rule 14).

